                                  Keyboard / Mouse Not Working – Troubleshooting



      Check Physical Connections
Check to make sure keyboard and mouse are properly plugged in
Try a different USB port
Don't use USB hubs; connect directly to the PC


      Test with Another Device
Test keyboard/mouse on other computer
Try a known-working keyboard or mouse on the affected PC


      Check for Power or Wireless Issues
For wireless devices:
Check batteries
Ensure the USB receiver is connected
Turn the device on/off


For wired devices:
Check for damaged cables


      Restart the Computer
Restart Windows to reload device drivers
Temporary driver or USB errors may be cleared after restart


    Check Device Manager
Open Device Manager
Expand Keyboards and Mice and other pointing devices
Look for warning icons "caution icon"
Right-click device: Properties to check device status


Update or Reinstall Drivers
Right click device: Update driver
If issue continues:
Right click device: Uninstall device
Restart PC to allow Windows to reinstall the driver


      Check USB Controllers
In Device Manager, expand Universal Serial Bus controllers
Check for errors or disabled devices
Restart USB Root Hub if needed


      (If Devices Don’t Work at Boot)
If keyboard or mouse does not work before Windows loads:


Possible USB support disabled in BIOS
Ensure USB Legacy Support is enabled
BIOS changes require system restart
